/*
We have 3N cards.
Operation (done N-1 times):
- Take the leftmost 5 cards, reorder them arbitrarily.
- Remove the leftmost 3 cards.
Score +1 if those removed 3 are equal.
After N-1 operations, 3 cards remain; +1 if they are equal.

Key observation:
At any step, among the first 5 cards we may choose ANY 3 to remove (order irrelevant),
because we can reorder arbitrarily before removing the leftmost 3.
So the process is:
Starting from the left, maintain 2 carried cards. At each step, add next 3 cards,
forming a multiset of 5 cards; choose any 3 to remove, keep 2 for next step.

DP on the pair of carried cards.
State after processing first 3t cards removed and carrying 2 cards to the front of the rest.
Initially after looking at first 5 cards, choose 3 removed and 2 carried.
Then each transition consumes next 3 original cards.

Let dp[a][b] = max score so far when current carried pair is (a,b), unordered.
Values are 1..N, number of states O(N^2). Transition per state considers the 10 ways
to choose 3 removed from 5 cards. Total O(N^2 * N) too big if done naively over all pairs,
but only reachable states matter.

We store sparse states in unordered_map / vector of pairs.
From one state and incoming triple, only 10 transitions.

Number of reachable states can still grow to O(N^2), which is fine for N up to a few thousands,
but problem statement gives no bounds. We can do better reasoning:

State is just an unordered pair from values 1..N => at most N(N+1)/2.
Transitions are tiny. This is usually acceptable in C++ for N around 2000.
Without bounds, this is the intended DP.

Implementation detail:
Represent unordered pair (x,y) with x<=y encoded as x*(N+1)+y.
Use unordered_map<int,int> for sparse DP each layer.
For each state, combine with incoming triple c,d,e and enumerate all 10 choices of kept pair.
Equivalent easier: enumerate all pairs among the 5 cards to keep (10 choices); removed are other 3.
Gain if removed three equal.

Final step:
After all N-1 removals, we have a carried pair plus last original card? Let's index carefully.

Initially cards = 3N.
Each operation removes 3 and keeps 2 from first 5, effectively advancing by 3 new cards each time after the first.
Model:
Start with first 5 cards.
Choose 3 removed, keep 2.
Then for op 2, add cards 6..8.
...
After N-1 operations, we've consumed 5 + 3*(N-2) = 3N-1 cards and keep 2 cards;
the last remaining 3 cards are these 2 plus card 3N.
Thus after processing transitions up to adding triples ending at card 3N-1, final score adds
1 if carried pair plus last card are all equal.

Special case N=1: no operations, just check the 3 cards.

Layer count:
If N>=2:
- Initialize from first 5 cards = indices [0..4], corresponding to first operation.
- For step s = 2..N-1, add next triple starting at index 5 + 3*(s-2).
- Final remaining last card is index 3N-1.

Check:
For N=2, initialize from first 5 cards (one operation), then final card index 5 => yes.

*/

static inline long long encodePair(int a, int b, int base) {
    if (a > b) swap(a, b);
    return 1LL * a * base + b;
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int N;
    cin >> N;
    vector<int> A(3 * N);
    for (int i = 0; i < 3 * N; ++i) cin >> A[i];

    if (N == 1) {
        cout << ((A[0] == A[1] && A[1] == A[2]) ? 1 : 0) << '\n';
        return 0;
    }

    const int BASE = N + 1;

    unordered_map<long long, int> dp, ndp;
    dp.reserve(1024);
    ndp.reserve(1024);

    // Initialize from first 5 cards: choose any 2 to keep.
    int init[5] = {A[0], A[1], A[2], A[3], A[4]};
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < 5; ++j) {
            vector<int> rem;
            rem.reserve(3);
            for (int k = 0; k < 5; ++k) {
                if (k != i && k != j) rem.push_back(init[k]);
            }
            int gain = (rem[0] == rem[1] && rem[1] == rem[2]) ? 1 : 0;
            int x = init[i], y = init[j];
            if (x > y) swap(x, y);
            long long key = encodePair(x, y, BASE);
            auto it = dp.find(key);
            if (it == dp.end()) dp.emplace(key, gain);
            else it->second = max(it->second, gain);
        }
    }

    // Steps 2..N-1
    for (int step = 2; step <= N - 1; ++step) {
        int pos = 5 + 3 * (step - 2);
        int add[3] = {A[pos], A[pos + 1], A[pos + 2]};
        ndp.clear();
        ndp.reserve(dp.size() * 2 + 16);

        for (auto &entry : dp) {
            long long key = entry.first;
            int cur = entry.second;
            int x = key / BASE;
            int y = key % BASE;

            int five[5] = {x, y, add[0], add[1], add[2]};

            // choose any 2 of 5 to keep
            for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
                for (int j = i + 1; j < 5; ++j) {
                    int rem[3], t = 0;
                    for (int k = 0; k < 5; ++k) {
                        if (k != i && k != j) rem[t++] = five[k];
                    }
                    int gain = (rem[0] == rem[1] && rem[1] == rem[2]) ? 1 : 0;
                    int a = five[i], b = five[j];
                    if (a > b) swap(a, b);
                    long long nkey = encodePair(a, b, BASE);
                    int val = cur + gain;
                    auto it = ndp.find(nkey);
                    if (it == ndp.end()) ndp.emplace(nkey, val);
                    else if (val > it->second) it->second = val;
                }
            }
        }

        dp.swap(ndp);
    }

    int last = A[3 * N - 1];
    int ans = 0;
    for (auto &entry : dp) {
        long long key = entry.first;
        int cur = entry.second;
        int x = key / BASE;
        int y = key % BASE;
        if (x == y && y == last) cur++;
        ans = max(ans, cur);
    }

    cout << ans << '\n';
    return 0;
}

