/*
We have 3N cards, values in [1..N].

Operation repeated N-1 times:
- Take the leftmost 5 cards, permute them arbitrarily,
- Remove the leftmost 3.
Gain 1 iff the removed 3 are equal.
After that, 3 cards remain; gain 1 iff those 3 are equal.

Key observation:
At every step, among the first 5 cards, we may choose any 3 to remove, and the remaining 2 stay in order relative only as "the 2 survivors", then 3 new cards arrive from the right. Since permutation is arbitrary, only the multiset of the current 5 matters.

DP on the first two "carried" cards before each step.
Initially, before step 1, carried cards are the first 2 cards a[0], a[1], and the 3 incoming are a[2],a[3],a[4].
After each step, 2 survivors remain and next 3 cards enter.

State:
dp[x][y] = max score after processing some number of blocks, where the current remaining 2 cards are values x,y (unordered enough, but we store ordered pair as read from chosen survivors; order does not matter for transitions, yet keeping both is fine).

More precisely, let blocks t = 0..N-2 correspond to operations.
Before operation t, current 5 cards are:
carry pair + cards at positions 2+3t, 3+3t, 4+3t.
Choose any 3 to remove; if equal => +1.
The remaining 2 become next carry.

After N-1 operations, exactly 3 cards remain: the final carry pair plus last incoming card? Let's index carefully.

Initially 3N cards.
Each op removes 3, so after N-1 ops, 3 cards remain.

If we think:
Before op 0: positions 0..4 are available, carry = a0,a1 and incoming triple = a2,a3,a4.
After op 0, survivors 2 plus next triple a5,a6,a7 form next 5.
...
Before op t: carry + a[3t+2], a[3t+3], a[3t+4]
for t=0..N-2. Correct, since last t=N-2 uses a[3N-4],a[3N-3],a[3N-2].
After that op, 2 survivors remain, and there is one final unseen card a[3N-1] to make total 3 remaining.
So final score adds 1 if survivors + a[3N-1] are all equal.

Transition from 5 cards:
Enumerate all pairs of survivors (i,j), remove other 3.
Score add = 1 if removed 3 equal.

State count N<=? not given, but values in [1..N], so pair DP size O(N^2). Transitions per state 10 survivor pairs. Total O(N^3) if all states active. This is likely too much if N large.

Need optimize using sparsity? Number of reachable pairs may still be O(N^2). But maybe N moderate. Since no constraints, safer approach:
At each step, only values among processed prefix matter, but still many.

Alternative: transition depends only on 5 multiset. Yet from pair + triple, 10 choices.

We'll implement hash map DP over reachable pairs. In many practical cases okay. Use long key = x*(N+1)+y. Since order irrelevant, canonically sort pair (min,max) because survivors are unordered for future. This halves states and is valid because next step depends only multiset of 5.

Transition:
given pair (u,v) and triple (p,q,r), form arr[5].
For each survivor pair indices i<j:
  s1=arr[i], s2=arr[j], sort
  removed are other 3; if equal add1.
Take max.

Initial dp has one state: sorted(a0,a1) with score 0.
Process N-1 ops.
Then finalize with last card a[3N-1]: for each pair, if both equal last card add1.

Special case N=1: no operations, just check all 3 cards equal.

Use HashMap<Long,Integer> current/next.
*/
public class Main {
    static long key(int a, int b) {
        if (a > b) { int t = a; a = b; b = t; }
        return (((long) a) << 32) ^ (b & 0xffffffffL);
    }

    static int keyA(long k) { return (int) (k >> 32); }
    static int keyB(long k) { return (int) k; }

    static void upd(HashMap<Long, Integer> map, long k, int v) {
        Integer old = map.get(k);
        if (old == null || v > old) map.put(k, v);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        int N = fs.nextInt();
        int[] a = new int[3 * N];
        for (int i = 0; i < 3 * N; i++) a[i] = fs.nextInt();

        if (N == 1) {
            System.out.println((a[0] == a[1] && a[1] == a[2]) ? 1 : 0);
            return;
        }

        HashMap<Long, Integer> dp = new HashMap<>();
        dp.put(key(a[0], a[1]), 0);

        for (int t = 0; t <= N - 2; t++) {
            int p = a[3 * t + 2];
            int q = a[3 * t + 3];
            int r = a[3 * t + 4];

            HashMap<Long, Integer> ndp = new HashMap<>();

            for (Map.Entry<Long, Integer> e : dp.entrySet()) {
                int u = keyA(e.getKey());
                int v = keyB(e.getKey());
                int base = e.getValue();

                int[] arr = {u, v, p, q, r};

                for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
                    for (int j = i + 1; j < 5; j++) {
                        int s1 = arr[i], s2 = arr[j];
                        int x = -1, y = -1, z = -1, cnt = 0;
                        for (int k = 0; k < 5; k++) {
                            if (k == i || k == j) continue;
                            if (cnt == 0) x = arr[k];
                            else if (cnt == 1) y = arr[k];
                            else z = arr[k];
                            cnt++;
                        }
                        int add = (x == y && y == z) ? 1 : 0;
                        upd(ndp, key(s1, s2), base + add);
                    }
                }
            }

            dp = ndp;
        }

        int last = a[3 * N - 1];
        int ans = 0;
        for (Map.Entry<Long, Integer> e : dp.entrySet()) {
            int u = keyA(e.getKey());
            int v = keyB(e.getKey());
            int cur = e.getValue();
            if (u == v && v == last) cur++;
            ans = Math.max(ans, cur);
        }

        System.out.println(ans);
    }

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do c = read(); while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            int val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }
}
